  "notes": "Theory-of-change builder ('Throughline'). Canvas is a strict five-column logic model (Inputs → Activities → Outputs → Short & mid-term → Long-term outcomes) crossed by three tinted program swimlanes with vertical rotated uppercase labels (blue tutoring, purple shared, orange summer). Node cards have a thick colored left border by program; edges are smooth bezier curves in program color, with dashed amber lines for weak evidence and dotted lines for split-copied links; small circular A/E/! markers sit on edges for assumptions, external factors and weak-evidence flags. Outcome nodes carry indicator/evidence count chips and SHORT/MID horizon tags plus amber 'Needs target'/'No indicator' pills. A '15 line crossings' red pill quantifies layout quality next to Auto-arrange. Right panel is a grant-readiness checklist with a pale-teal deadline card in serif. Warm off-white paper palette with deep teal brand. Filed proposal for node-editor values: causal-logic-model semantics, column-and-swimlane-slots arrangement, column-add-button."
